# The read under the key of a for-in goes by the enumerator's index behind a test. Where nothing has run since the step, the test takes the step's word: the index of the name lies below the count of names that the step found current.
# Here a call stands between the step and the read, and it deletes the very name: the test asks the object itself, fails, and the read goes as it is written: undefined.
# THE LIE, testing=KeysOfForInAreTakenToBeAsTheStepFoundThem: the test takes the step's word though other code has run. NO RUN UNDER THE LIE ALONE IS STORED: the read would take the cleared slot of the deleted name for a value.
# Under --aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges (testing=TestsEveryPosition) the read holds the object's structure and order word against the enumerator's, or the process stops by name.
# RUN(TAKEN): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# TAKEN-NOT: IsEnumeratorCurrent {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}} traits
# TAKEN: EnumeratorGetByVal
# RUN(LIED): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all testing=KeysOfForInAreTakenToBeAsTheStepFoundThem
# LIED: IsEnumeratorCurrent {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}} traits
# LIED: EnumeratorGetByVal
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition
# RIGHT: ash1birch2cedar_date4elm5fir6gum7hazel8
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=KeysOfForInAreTakenToBeAsTheStepFoundThem,TestsEveryPosition
# HELD: AOT: f{{*}}
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
